{
	"_comment": "Parameter-domain scope planning, replayed by _shared/lua/test/config_scope_plan_contract.lua on macOS and Linux. entry points: scope_inventory(scope, {actions = <function answering the stored action_parameters paths>}, owners) and scope_plan(scope, mode, paths, owners) of the manifest reader, where owners.action_parameter_domain(path) answers the domain of a path \"action_parameters.<domain>__<binding>__<action>\" (the domain is one of gesture, keyboard, script, tap_key, tap_hold) only when <binding> is lowercase letters, digits and single underscores, never starting or ending with one, and <action> is a generated action that declares a parameter; otherwise it answers nothing. inventories: for each scope, the stored paths below and the number of paths the scope owns (inventory_count); for both modes \"clear\" and \"recommended\" the plan deletes exactly the inventory's paths as action_parameters rows (delete = true, no value). refusals: each path, given alone to scope_inventory and scope_plan of the gestures scope, makes both refuse (raise). declaration_plans: a declaration {features, scopes} is built with the config defaults contract (config_defaults.new), then direct_scope_plan(scope, mode, paths, owners) and scope_plan are asked: direct_presets are the presets of the direct plan, scope_preset_count the presets of the full plan, absent lists \"section.key\" rows the plan must not contain, deleted rows that are deletions, restored_not_deleted rows that are present and not deletions, set rows rewritten to a value. declaration_refusals: the call raises (with_owners passes the parameter-domain owner). declaration_cycles: foreign, cyclic or missing includes are not traversed by the direct plan (direct_operations rows) and the full plan raises. inventory_collections: the manifest reader's scope_inventory(scope, providers) where each provider is a function answering paths; calls is how many providers ran, owned the sorted unique paths the scope owns, and the clear plan over them deletes each one with the quoted section spelling in section_of and no row for no_row_for. inventory_refusals: scope_inventory raises (a provider with raises raises, with not_a_function is not callable).",
	"drivers": {
		"macos": "Replays every vector.",
		"linux": "Replays every vector.",
		"windows": "Not ported: one AHK consumer calls the Windows manifest reader's scope inventory and plan with an owner built from the generated action catalogue."
	},
